# Rhyme-SHAKE Optimized Implementation

## Targets

- `make` → `KAT_SIG` — default optimized build, KAT byte-identical to Reference
- `make fast` → `KAT_SIG_FAST` — USE_DP1_CHECK enabled for faster key generation

## KAT Compatibility

The default target (`make`) produces KAT output byte-identical to the Reference
implementation test vectors.

The fast target (`make fast`) enables `-DUSE_DP1_CHECK` which uses a faster
coprimality test during key generation.  This may produce a different valid
secret basis, resulting in different KAT bytes.  However, all generated
signatures self-verify correctly, and the algorithm semantics are unchanged.

## DP1 Fast Keygen

`USE_DP1_CHECK` switches the keygen solver from the default order-(D-1) minor
descent to an order-d "truncated tail columns" coprimality check.  Per the
source code, this is a "sound sufficient test (monotone gcd ideal)" that
provides approximately 8-14x keygen speedup for higher security levels.
